@startuml 19_act_attribute_lifecycle
!include _style.iuml
title New attribute: from a free question to a category definition shared with all hospitals

' declare swimlanes in reading order
|Purchaser client (hospital A)|
|Hub|
|LLM|
|Supplier user|
|Hub operator (curator)|
|Hospital nodes (via each client)|
|Purchaser client (hospital A)|
start
:Add free question in review step\n"Does the pack include a peel-off\ndocumentation label?" (attribute_key NULL);
|Hub|
:Question DRAFT; attribute_proposals PENDING;\nenqueue PROPOSE_ATTRIBUTE;
|LLM|
:propose_attribute (Sonnet 5):\nquestion + category template + registry keys;
note right
  Output has no criticality field.
  Labels must be neutral (validator rejects
  tenant names, aliases, brands, products).
end note
|Hub|
if (Asks for a product number?) then (IDENTIFIER)
  :Question takes the identifier definition\n(kind = IDENTIFIER); proposal ROUTED;
  :Answer becomes an identifier fact:\nno criticality, never in a template,\nnever compared (D50, D51);
  stop
elseif (Matches an existing attribute?) then (yes)
  :Question gets the existing key;\nproposal MATCHED;
  :Normal question flow;
  stop
else (no)
  :Proposal NEW: peel_off_label, bool,\nDE/EN labels; question expected_answer typed;
endif
|Purchaser client (hospital A)|
:POST send-questions\n(409 while any proposal is PENDING);
|Hub|
if (Question withdrawn before sending?) then (yes)
  :Proposal discarded; no attribute created;
  stop
else (no)
  :attribute_definitions row PROVISIONAL;\nquestion SENT with attribute_key peel_off_label;
endif
|Supplier user|
:Answer "yes", applies to whole family;
|Hub|
:item_facts (FAMILY scope, SUPPLIER_ANSWER);\nREBUILD_PROJECTION -> additional_attributes;
:Visible to ALL hospitals as additional information\n(catalog, search candidates, comparison views);\nnot filtered, not judged, never auto-asked;
|Hub operator (curator)|
:Review proposal;
if (Decision?) then (approve)
  :Correct labels / synonyms if needed (neutral-label check);\nset CRITICALITY (e.g. major) and comparison rule;\nset shareable flag;
  :Add to the syringe_single_use definition;\nnew definition_hash, updated_at;
elseif (Decision?) then (merge)
  :Merge into an APPROVED attribute of the same type:\nevery value validated first (422 lists misfits, nothing moves);\nfacts re-added under the target key, old ones superseded;\nquestions take the target key; merged_into set, DEPRECATED;
else (reject)
  :Reject with a note:\nattribute DEPRECATED; facts kept for audit;\nfamilies re-projected, the information disappears;
endif
:Operator action written to operator_actions (audit);
if (Definition changed?) then (yes)
  |Hub|
  :attribute APPROVED; definition served
  by GET /templates (no signing, D52);
  |Hospital nodes (via each client)|
  :After token exchange: compare updated_at;\nfetch definition; PUT /templates at node;
  :Validate against the core model, store,\nrebuild category projections;
  :peel_off_label now in unknown_attributes\n(unless in EGRESS_DENY_ATTRIBUTES);
  |Hub|
  :New assessments: major UNKNOWN on the hospital side\n-> PURCHASER question; BD value already known -> BD not asked;
  :Open assessments pick it up next round;\nrounds already judged keep their stored definition;
else (no)
endif
stop

@enduml
